<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osian</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osian is an ancient town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thar-desert">Thar Desert</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, once an important trading centre on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a>. It is known for a group of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> and Jain temples built from the eighth to the twelfth century, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahavira">Mahavira</a> temple, dated to the time of the Pratihara king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vatsaraja">Vatsaraja</a>, and the Sachiya Mata temple. They are among the finest early examples of the western Indian temple style.</p></div>
